From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: xorbidden <xorbidden@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:34:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] xnu-deps: provide python for XNU's lldbmacros on python3-only
 hosts

XNU installs its lldb macros through core/syntax_checker.py, which
starts with "#!/usr/bin/env python". Debian and Ubuntu ship only
python3, so every macro file fails to install and make-kernel.sh
rejects the build although the kernel itself links. Add a host shim
that runs python3, next to the other host tools.

Tested: make kernel succeeds on Ubuntu 26.04 (python3 only).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .gitignore               | 1 +
 xnu-deps/host/bin/python | 3 +++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)
 create mode 100755 xnu-deps/host/bin/python

diff --git a/.gitignore b/.gitignore
index 51680ca..1b574b0 100644
--- a/.gitignore
+++ b/.gitignore
@@ -80,6 +80,7 @@ __pycache__/
 !/xnu-deps/host/bin/iig
 !/xnu-deps/host/bin/install
 !/xnu-deps/host/bin/plutil
+!/xnu-deps/host/bin/python
 !/xnu-deps/host/bin/sw_vers
 !/xnu-deps/host/bin/xcrun
 !/xnu-deps/host/bin/xnu-clang
diff --git a/xnu-deps/host/bin/python b/xnu-deps/host/bin/python
new file mode 100755
index 0000000..18c84d0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/xnu-deps/host/bin/python
@@ -0,0 +1,3 @@
+#!/bin/sh
+# XNU's lldbmacros syntax checker starts with "#!/usr/bin/env python"; hosts with only python3 (Debian, Ubuntu) have none
+exec python3 "$@"
